casimirProjection -- projection operator to a specified eigenspace of the Casimir operator
******************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        casimirProjection(rho,z)
  * Inputs:
      * rho, an instance of the type *note LieAlgebraRepresentation:
        LieAlgebraRepresentation,,
      * z, a *note rational number: (Macaulay2Doc)QQ,, 
  * Outputs:
      * M, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, 

Description
===========

Let $\rho$ be a LieAlgebraRepresentation, and recall the definition of the
Casimir operator from *note casimirOperator: casimirOperator,.



This function returns the projection matrix to the eigenspace of the Casimir
operator for the input eigenvalue z.  This matrix is computed as the product of
factors $\operatorname{Cas}-x I$ over all eigenvalues $x \neq z$.



