character -- Computes the character of a Lie algebra module
***********************************************************

  * Usage: 
        character V
  * Inputs:
      * V, an instance of the type *note LieAlgebraModule: LieAlgebraModule,, 
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Strategy => ..., default value null
  * Outputs:
      * C, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, 

Description
===========

An optional argument "Strategy" allows to specify which algorithm to use:
"Freudenthal" for Freudenthal's recursive algorithm; see Humphreys,
Introduction to Lie Algebras and Representation Theory, Section 22.3. "Weyl"
for Weyl's character formula (in classical types). "JacobiTrudi" and
"JacobiTrudi'" for Jacobi-Trudi and dual Jacobi-Trudi formulae (in type A).

See also
========

  * *note weightDiagram: weightDiagram, -- computes the weights in a Lie
    algebra module and their multiplicities

