deGraafRepresentation -- compute the representation with the specified highest weight using de Graaf's algorithm
****************************************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        deGraafRepresentation(lambda,g)
  * Inputs:
      * lambda, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, 
      * g, an instance of the type *note LieAlgebra: LieAlgebra,, 
  * Outputs:
      * rho, an instance of the type *note LieAlgebraRepresentation:
        LieAlgebraRepresentation,,

Description
===========

Let $V$ be an irreducible $\mathfrak{g}$-module with highest weight $\lamdba$.
Then $V$ may be constructed as follows. Let $U(\mathfrak{g})$ be the universal
enveloping algebra of $\mathfrak{g}$ (see *note universalEnvelopingAlgebra:
universalEnvelopingAlgebra,. Let $A(\lambda)$ be the (infinite-dimensional)
Verma module $U(\mathfrak{g})/J$, where $J$ is the left ideal $\{
x_1,\ldots,x_l,h_1-\lambda(H_1),\ldots,h_n-\lambda(H_n)\rangle$.  Then $V \cong
A(\lambda)/I$, and the action of $X \in \mathfrak{g}$ on elements of the basis
of $U(N^{-})/I$ is left multiplication.

We cannot implement the algorithm outlined above in a naive way because the
*note AssociativeAlgebras: (AssociativeAlgebras)Top, package does not currently
support quotients of quotients of free algebras.  Instead, following de Graaf,
we exploit the isomorphism $A(\lambda) \cong U(N^{-})$, and proceed as follows.

$\quad$ 1. We create $U(\mathfrak{g})$ and $U(N^{-})$ (see *note
universalEnvelopingAlgebra: universalEnvelopingAlgebra, and *note uNminus:
uNminus,)

$\quad$ 2. We compute the Gröbner basis $G$ of $I$, and a basis of the quotient
$U(N^{-})/I$ (see *note deGraafBases: deGraafBases,)

$\quad$ 3. For each $X$ in a basis of $\mathfrak{g}$, and each $B_i$ in de
Graaf's basis of $V$:

$\quad$$\quad$ a. Multiply $X.B_i$ in $U(\mathfrak{g})$

$\quad$$\quad$ b. Map this to $U(N^{-})$ under the map sending $x_i \mapsto 0$
and $h_i \mapsto h_i-\lambda(h_i)$

$\quad$$\quad$ c. At top level, we reduce by $I$ in $U(N^{-})$.

$\quad$ This gives the action of $X$ on de Graaf's basis of $V$. We extract the
coefficients to build the matrix.



