LieAlgebra ++ LieAlgebra -- Take the direct sum of Lie algebras
***************************************************************

  * Operator: *note ++: (Macaulay2Doc)++,

Description
===========

Starting from simple Lie algebras, one can take direct sums and produce
semi-simple ones:

+-------------------------------+
|i1 : g=simpleLieAlgebra("D",4);|
+-------------------------------+
|i2 : h=simpleLieAlgebra("G",2);|
+-------------------------------+
|i3 : g++h                      |
|                               |
|o3 = 𝔡  ++ 𝔤                   |
|      4     2                  |
|                               |
|o3 : LieAlgebra                |
+-------------------------------+
|i4 : directSum(g,g,h)          |
|                               |
|o4 = 𝔡  ++ 𝔡  ++ 𝔤             |
|      4     4     2            |
|                               |
|o4 : LieAlgebra                |
+-------------------------------+

Note that this is external direct sum, so if $g_i$ is a sub-Lie algebra of
$h_i$, $i=1,2$, then $g_1\oplus g_2$ is a sub-Lie algebra of $h_1\oplus h_2$.

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note LieAlgebra ++ LieAlgebra: LieAlgebra ++ LieAlgebra, -- Take the
    direct sum of Lie algebras
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

