lieAlgebraBasis -- computes an enhanced basis for a simple Lie algebra
**********************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        lieAlgebraBasis("A",2)
  * Inputs:
      * t, a *note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String,, 
      * m, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 
      * Method, a *note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String,, 
      * Check, a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, 
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Check
      * Method
  * Outputs:
      * LAB, an instance of the type *note LieAlgebraBasis: LieAlgebraBasis,, 

Description
===========

See *note LieAlgebraBasis: LieAlgebraBasis, for more details and references.

The optional argument "Method" may be set to "Lusztig" for the Lusztig
canonical basis, or "FH" for the basis described in Fulton-Harris,
Representation Theory: A First Course. The default is "FH" for types A, B, C,
D, and G.

The optional argument "Check" (default: true) runs a suite of tests on the
basis constructed. See the unexported function "checkLieAlgebraBasis" in the
package code for more details.

The user may either input the type and rank, or the simple Lie algebra.

