LieAlgebraModule @ LieAlgebraModule -- Take the tensor product of modules over different Lie algebras
*****************************************************************************************************

  * Operator: *note @: (Macaulay2Doc)@,

Description
===========

Produces a module over the direct sum of the Lie algebras of the two modules.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : LL_(1,2,3,4) (simpleLieAlgebra("D",4)) @ LL_(5,6)                       |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = LL           (𝔡  ++ 𝔤 )                                                 |
|       1,2,3,4,5,6  4     2                                                  |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : irreducible LieAlgebraModule over 𝔡  ++ 𝔤                               |
|                                        4     2                              |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|(simpleLieAlgebra("G",2))                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

A complicated way to define usual tensor product *note LieAlgebraModule **
LieAlgebraModule: LieAlgebraModule _st_st LieAlgebraModule, would be using the
diagonal embedding:

+-----------------------------------------------+
|i2 : g := simpleLieAlgebra("A",1)              |
|                                               |
|o2 = 𝔞                                         |
|      1                                        |
|                                               |
|o2 : simple LieAlgebra                         |
+-----------------------------------------------+
|i3 : h := g ++ g                               |
|                                               |
|o3 = 𝔞  ++ 𝔞                                   |
