VInSymdW -- computes a basis of a submodule of $\operatorname{Sym}^d W$ isomorphic to $V$ with a given highest weight vector
****************************************************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        VInSymdW(V,d,W,hwv)
  * Inputs:
      * V, an instance of the type *note LieAlgebraRepresentation:
        LieAlgebraRepresentation,,
      * d, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 
      * W, an instance of the type *note LieAlgebraRepresentation:
        LieAlgebraRepresentation,,
      * hwv, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, 
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * SaveAsFunction
  * Outputs:
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, 

Description
===========

Suppose that an irreducible module $V$ appears in the decomposition of
$\operatorname{Sym}^d W$ with multiplicity at least one. Then we can find a
highest weight vector using *note weightMuHighestWeightVectorsInSymdW:
weightMuHighestWeightVectorsInSymdW,, and then compute a basis of a submodule
in $\operatorname{Sym}^d W$ isomorphic to $V$. The basis elements are expressed
as polynomials in the basis of $W$ used to define the matrix generators of the
representation on $W$.



We compute the degree four invariant for plane cubics by finding a trivial
submodule in $\operatorname{Sym}^4 \operatorname{Sym}^3 \mathbb{C}^3$.



+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : sl3=simpleLieAlgebra("A",2)                                             |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = sl3                                                                     |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : simple LieAlgebra                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : V=standardRepresentation(sl3);                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : S3V = symmetricPower(3,V);                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : hwv = weightMuHighestWeightVectorsInSymdW({0,0},4,S3V);                 |
